From: acww-3ds <noreply@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Nook's: "Nook's without multiplayer" (option
 ACWW_NOOK_SOLO)

From AC:WW+ (github.com/migueliranzo/acww-plus, MIT). Nookway becomes Nookington's only after a visitor from another
town bought something (save flag 7, NookShop_HasVisitorBought); with the option the sales alone do it
(NookShop_GetEarnedLevel, whose callers schedule the remodel). And NookShop_UpdateDaily rolls the sale day, the
evening sale and the spotlight item only in towns of two or more residents; with the option one is enough. The other
condition stays: a resident who finished Nook's part-time job (player flag 1 clear). Off, the game's.
---
 src/main/unk_020ac750.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main/unk_020ac750.cpp b/src/main/unk_020ac750.cpp
index da04680..6c421e1 100644
--- a/src/main/unk_020ac750.cpp
+++ b/src/main/unk_020ac750.cpp
@@ -1,4 +1,7 @@
 #include "uptr.h"
+#ifdef ENHANCED_PORT
+#include "port_options.h"
+#endif
 #include "host_labels.h"
 // mwcc-flags: -str reuse
 #include "types.h"
@@ -892,6 +895,9 @@ extern "C" int NookShop_GetEarnedLevel(NookShop *self) {
     if (self->sales >= NookShop_GetUpgradeSales(self, t)) {
         int r = NookShop_HasVisitorBought(&data_021ed104);
         if (t == 2) {
+#ifdef ENHANCED_PORT
+            if (port_nook_solo()) r = 1;  // ("Nook's without multiplayer": no visitor's purchase needed)
+#endif
             if (r != 0) return t + 1;
         } else {
             return t + 1;
@@ -1017,7 +1023,12 @@ extern "C" void NookShop_UpdateDaily(NookShop *self, int force) {
     NookShop_Restock(self, d.year, d.month, d.day);
     ok = 1;
     int cnt = PlayerDataArray_CountUsed(gSavePlayers);
+#ifdef ENHANCED_PORT
+    // ("Nook's without multiplayer": one resident is enough; one who finished Nook's part-time job is still needed)
+    if (cnt != 0 && (cnt != 1 || port_nook_solo())) {
+#else
     if (cnt != 0 && cnt != 1) {
+#endif
         for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
             p = PlayerData_GetResident(gSavePlayers, i);
             if (p != 0 && ((PlayerData *)(p))->isUsed() != 0 && ((PlayerData *)(p))->testFlag(1) == 0) {
